  <itemBody><p>A garden-data item asks the student to match observations with reasonable interpretations.</p><matchInteraction responseIdentifier="RESPONSE"><prompt>Match each observation from a community garden study with the most reasonable interpretation.</prompt><simpleMatchSet><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="A" matchMax="1">Mulched beds stayed moist two days longer after watering.</simpleAssociableChoice><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="B" matchMax="1">Uncovered beds had more weeds by the third week.</simpleAssociableChoice><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="C" matchMax="1">Beds near the fence received less afternoon sun.</simpleAssociableChoice><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="D" matchMax="1">The garden sign was repainted on Saturday.</simpleAssociableChoice></simpleMatchSet><simpleMatchSet><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="G1" matchMax="1">Mulch helped reduce water loss from the soil.</simpleAssociableChoice><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="G2" matchMax="1">Bare soil may need more frequent weeding.</simpleAssociableChoice><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="G3" matchMax="1">Light exposure was not identical across all beds.</simpleAssociableChoice><simpleAssociableChoice identifier="G4" matchMax="1">This maintenance detail does not explain plant growth.</simpleAssociableChoice></simpleMatchSet></matchInteraction></itemBody>
  <responseProcessing template="http://www.imsglobal.org/question/qti_v2p1/rptemplates/match_correct"/>
</assessmentItem>",
}
`;

